// APNT settlement authorization covenant (SAC) v0.
//
// Maturity: frozen — this redeem-script bytecode is disassembled and matched
// byte-for-byte, including L_verdict, by
// `npm run verify:settlement-authorization-covenant-independent`. See
// AGENTS.md, "The maturity ladder".
//
// Target architecture:
// openspec/changes/define-apnt-private-spend-covenant-v0/design.md
//   §1.1.3 (properties B and C), as corrected by
//   §1.1.5 ("Measured correction") and
//   §1.1.6a ("Measured correction and decisions, recorded 2026-08-05").
//
// This is the redeem script of the P2SH32 program `L_verdict` that spends the
// chunked verifier's terminal verdict token. It reconstructs the canonical
// `APNTTSP0` settlement-projection transcript from transaction introspection
// alone and requires its domain-separated SHA-256 to equal the verdict NFT's
// own commitment. That is what carries "this transaction is the transaction
// the proven statement authorizes" onto the chain.
//
// The transcript layout reproduced below is byte-exact with
// `serializeAPNTTransitionSettlementProjectionV0`
// (../apnt_transition_settlement_projection_v0.ts). All integers are
// little-endian, matching that module's `writeU32LE` / `writeU64LE`.
//
//   "APNTTSP0" || 0x00                       9 constant bytes
//   u32le(transactionVersion)                OP_TXVERSION
//   u32le(locktime)                          OP_TXLOCKTIME
//   u32le(inputCount)                        OP_TXINPUTCOUNT
//   u32le(designatedVerifierInputIndex)      OP_INPUTINDEX
//   for each input i != OP_INPUTINDEX:
//     OP_OUTPOINTTXHASH(i)                   32 bytes, already wire order
//     u32le(OP_OUTPOINTINDEX(i))
//     u32le(OP_INPUTSEQUENCENUMBER(i))
//     u64le(OP_UTXOVALUE(i))
//   u32le(outputCount)                       OP_TXOUTPUTCOUNT
//   for each output j:
//     require size(OP_OUTPUTTOKENCATEGORY(j)) == 0     token-free outputs
//     u64le(OP_OUTPUTVALUE(j))
//     u32le(size(OP_OUTPUTBYTECODE(j))) || OP_OUTPUTBYTECODE(j)
//   u64le(networkFeeSats)                    sum(OP_UTXOVALUE) - sum(OP_OUTPUTVALUE)
//
// then, per `sha256DomainSeparated` (../hash.ts):
//
//   SHA256( u16be(len(P)) || P || u16be(len(D)) || D || u32be(len(transcript))
//           || transcript )
//
// where P is this repository's fixed hash personalization and D is
// `bch-cloak-apnt-v0:transition-settlement-projection-commitment-v0`. The
// constant part `u16be(len(P)) || P || u16be(len(D)) || D` is 110 bytes and is
// substituted by the TypeScript builder into the domain-separation prefix
// marker below, derived from those real constants so it can never drift from
// `hash.ts`. Design.md's original "2+41+2+64 = 109" is wrong by one byte: the
// personalization is 42 bytes, not 41.
//
// ONE OP_SHA256, never OP_HASH256. `settlementProjection32` is a single
// domain-separated SHA-256, not a bare double hash. Using OP_HASH256 here
// yields an unspendable, unsound covenant.
//
// The SAC does NOT require itself to be the last input. The transcript commits
// `designatedVerifierInputIndex` as an explicit field, so this script reads
// OP_INPUTINDEX directly and is correct at any index (design.md §1.1.6a
// correction 5). It also does not check its own token category: authenticity of
// the verdict category is the seal's aggregate branch's job.
//
// Expected witness stack on entry: [] (the redeem script itself is the only
// unlocking push; this covenant takes no witness data).
//
// Fee accumulator convention: the running networkFeeSats total lives on the
// ALTSTACK for the whole unrolled region; the transcript accumulator is the
// single main-stack item. Because the transcript is one stack item, its length
// is capped by the VM's maximumStackItemLength (10,000 bytes on BCH 2026) —
// this, not script size or operation cost, is the ceiling that binds on batch
// shape (design.md §1.1.6a correction 4).
//
// This is a locking-template artifact. It is not APNT acceptance, lane
// advancement, note spendability, proof verification, or broadcast approval.

// --- transcript head: "APNTTSP0" || 0x00 ---
0x09 0x41504e545453503000

// --- u32le(transactionVersion), widened to 5 bytes then truncated because a
//     VM number at or above 2**31 needs a fifth sign byte ---
OP_TXVERSION <5> OP_NUM2BIN <4> OP_SPLIT OP_DROP OP_CAT

// --- u32le(locktime), same widening ---
OP_TXLOCKTIME <5> OP_NUM2BIN <4> OP_SPLIT OP_DROP OP_CAT

// --- u32le(inputCount), structurally small ---
OP_TXINPUTCOUNT <4> OP_NUM2BIN OP_CAT

// --- u32le(designatedVerifierInputIndex) ---
OP_INPUTINDEX <4> OP_NUM2BIN OP_CAT

// --- fee accumulator := 0, on the altstack ---
OP_0 OP_TOALTSTACK

// --- guarded, unrolled input loop (MAX_INPUTS slots) ---
@UNROLLED_INPUT_SLOTS@

// --- u32le(outputCount) ---
OP_TXOUTPUTCOUNT <4> OP_NUM2BIN OP_CAT

// --- guarded, unrolled output loop (MAX_OUTPUTS slots) ---
@UNROLLED_OUTPUT_SLOTS@

// --- u64le(networkFeeSats), from the altstack accumulator ---
OP_FROMALTSTACK <8> OP_NUM2BIN OP_CAT

// --- u32be(len(transcript)); OP_NUM2BIN is little-endian, so reverse it ---
OP_SIZE <4> OP_NUM2BIN OP_REVERSEBYTES

// --- the 110-byte domain-separation constant prefix ---
@DOMAIN_SEPARATION_PREFIX_PUSH@

// --- assemble prefix || u32be(len) || transcript, then hash once ---
OP_SWAP OP_CAT OP_SWAP OP_CAT
OP_SHA256

// --- require it to equal this input's own verdict-NFT commitment ---
OP_INPUTINDEX OP_UTXOTOKENCOMMITMENT OP_EQUAL
